            "type": "reasoning_text",
            "text": "The user is asking me to explain the idea of binary search in one sentence, in Chinese.\n\nBinary search: The core idea is to repeatedly divide the search interval in half by comparing the target value with the middle element of a sorted array, narrowing down to one half where the target could be, until found or the interval is empty.\n\nLet me craft a concise one-sentence answer in Chinese:\n\n二分查找的思想是：在一个有序数组中，每次将目标值与中间元素比较，从而排除一半的搜索范围，不断将查找区间折半缩小，直到找到目标或区间为空。\n\nThat's one sentence. Keep it brief since the request is for one sentence."
          }
